Imports:
  - Types:
      - Track AS DomainTrack
    From: domain/src/main/java/tachiyomi/domain/track/model
  - Types:
      - Manga
    From: domain/src/main/java/tachiyomi/domain/manga/model
  - Types:
      - Source
    From: source-api/src/main/kotlin/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/source

Usages:
  extension_point: |
    A new remote tracking service is added by implementing `Tracker` (typically by extending
    `BaseTracker`, which supplies the shared credential-storage/login-state/remote-update-dispatch
    plumbing so a concrete tracker only needs to fill in service-specific API calls, status
    lists, and score mapping), optionally also implementing `DeletableTracker` and/or
    `EnhancedTracker`, then registering one instance of it in `TrackerManager`'s trackers list
    with a stable, never-reused id.

Annotations: |
  This is Mihon's real, in-repo extension point for remote tracking services: eleven concrete
  trackers (not documented individually here) already follow this pattern, and `TrackerManager`
  is the fixed, statically-assembled registry every part of the app queries to find them — there
  is no dynamic/plugin-style loading here, unlike the external Source extension mechanism.

  Use `DomainTrack`/Manga/Source from Imports throughout.
  Use `extension_point` to add a new tracking service.

---

"Tracker()":
  location: Tracker.kt
  annotations: |
    Full contract a remote tracking service integration must satisfy: identity, login/session
    state, status/score vocabulary, and the read/update operations `TrackerManager` and
    tracking-related interactors drive.

    Use `extension_point`.
  properties:
    "id -> Long": |
      Unique, stable tracker id; also the value stored as DomainTrack.trackerId.
    "name -> String": |
      Tracker display name.
    "supportsReadingDates -> Boolean": |
      Whether this service can store start/finish reading dates.
    "supportsPrivateTracking -> Boolean": |
      Whether this service supports marking an entry private/hidden from public lists.
    "isLoggedIn -> Boolean": |
      Whether valid credentials are currently stored for this tracker.
    "isLoggedInFlow -> Flow<Boolean>": |
      Reactive equivalent of isLoggedIn.
  methods:
    "getStatusList() -> statuses:List<Long>": |
      Every status code this service supports, in display order.
    "getReadingStatus() -> status:Long": |
      The status code meaning "currently reading".
    "getRereadingStatus() -> status:Long": |
      The status code meaning "re-reading", if supported.
    "getCompletionStatus() -> status:Long": |
      The status code meaning "completed".
    "getScoreList() -> scores:List<String>": |
      Every score value this service accepts, as display strings, in ascending order.
    "get10PointScore(track: DomainTrack) -> score:Double": |
      track.score normalized to a common 0-10 scale for cross-tracker display.
    "indexToScore(index: Int) -> score:Double": |
      Map a getScoreList() index back to this service's native score value.
    "displayScore(track: DomainTrack) -> label:String": |
      Human-readable rendering of track.score in this service's own notation.
    "search(query: String) -> results:List<TrackSearch>": |
      Search the remote service for entries matching `query`, for the user to pick a bind
      target.
    "refresh(track: Track) -> refreshed:Track": |
      Re-fetch the current state of an already-bound entry from the remote service.
    "login(username: String, password: String)": |
      Authenticate and persist credentials for this service.
    "logout()": |
      Clear stored credentials for this service.
    "register(item: Track, mangaId: Long)": |
      Bind a manga to a newly-created or newly-matched remote entry.
    "setRemoteStatus(track: Track, status: Long)": |
      Push a status change to the remote service.
    "setRemoteLastChapterRead(track: Track, chapterNumber: Int)": |
      Push a reading-progress change to the remote service.
    "setRemoteScore(track: Track, scoreString: String)": |
      Push a score change, given as one of getScoreList()'s display strings, to the remote
      service.
    "setRemoteStartDate(track: Track, epochMillis: Long)": |
      Push a start-date change to the remote service; only meaningful when
      supportsReadingDates is true.
    "setRemoteFinishDate(track: Track, epochMillis: Long)": |
      Push a finish-date change to the remote service; only meaningful when
      supportsReadingDates is true.
    "setRemotePrivate(track: Track, private: Boolean)": |
      Push a privacy-flag change to the remote service; only meaningful when
      supportsPrivateTracking is true.

"Tracker::BaseTracker(id: Long, name: String)":
  location: BaseTracker.kt
  annotations: |
    Shared base implementation of `Tracker` that every concrete tracking-service integration
    extends, supplying credential storage, derived login state, and the common
    update-then-persist-locally flow so concrete subclasses implement only the remote API calls.

    id, name: identity, passed straight through to the `Tracker` properties of the same name

    Algorithm:
    1. isLoggedIn/isLoggedInFlow derive from whether stored username and password are both
       non-empty
    2. Each setRemote* method mutates the given track's local field, then calls the abstract
       update for the subclass to push it remotely, then persists the result locally
       (updateRemote) by converting it to a `DomainTrack` and inserting it, ignoring the
       failure (surfaced only as a toast) rather than propagating it
    3. logout() clears stored credentials; subclasses that override it must call the base
       implementation

    Use `extension_point`.

"DeletableTracker()":
  location: DeletableTracker.kt
  annotations: |
    Optional capability a `Tracker` additionally implements when its remote service supports
    removing an entry entirely, not just changing its status.
  methods:
    "delete(track: DomainTrack)": |
      Remove `track`'s entry from the remote service.

"EnhancedTracker()":
  location: EnhancedTracker.kt
  annotations: |
    Optional capability a `Tracker` additionally implements when it is tied to specific
    Sources and unique remote ids, so the app can auto-bind or auto-migrate tracking without
    prompting the user to search-and-match manually.

    Use Source from Imports for accept/isTrackFrom/migrateTrack.
  methods:
    "accept(source: Source) -> accepted:Boolean": |
      Whether this tracker is compatible with `source`, default implemented by checking
      `source`'s class name against getAcceptedSources().
    "getAcceptedSources() -> classNames:List<String>": |
      Fully-qualified class names of every Source this tracker is compatible with.
    "loginNoop()": |
      Perform whatever bookkeeping this tracker needs when it is "logged in" without a real
      user-driven login step (since enhanced trackers are tied to a source, not a user account).
    "match(manga: Manga) -> match:TrackSearch?": |
      Like Tracker.search, but returns at most one exact match for `manga`, since an enhanced
      tracker can identify the correct remote entry unambiguously.
    "isTrackFrom(track: DomainTrack, manga: Manga, source: Source?) -> matches:Boolean": |
      Whether `track` was created by this tracker for `manga` fetched from `source`.
    "migrateTrack(track: DomainTrack, manga: Manga, newSource: Source) -> migrated:DomainTrack?": |
      Re-point `track` to the equivalent entry for `manga` under `newSource`, or null if this
      tracker cannot resolve one.

"TrackerManager()":
  location: TrackerManager.kt
  annotations: |
    Fixed, statically-assembled registry of every tracker instance the app supports.

    Algorithm:
    1. Every supported tracker is constructed once as a val and collected into the trackers
       list, each with a hardcoded, never-reused id
    2. loggedInTrackers/loggedInTrackersFlow filter trackers by Tracker.isLoggedIn/
       isLoggedInFlow
    3. get/getAll look up trackers by id against the fixed trackers list

    Use `extension_point` for how a new tracker joins this list.
  properties:
    "trackers -> List<Tracker>": |
      Every tracker instance the app supports, construction order.
  methods:
    "loggedInTrackers() -> trackers:List<Tracker>": |
      Trackers with valid stored credentials.
    "loggedInTrackersFlow() -> trackers:Flow<List<Tracker>>": |
      Reactive equivalent of loggedInTrackers.
    "get(id: Long) -> tracker:Tracker?": |
      The tracker with the given id, or null if no tracker is registered under it.
    "getAll(ids: Set<Long>) -> trackers:List<Tracker>": |
      Every registered tracker whose id is in `ids`.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Mihon's genuine in-repo extension point for remote tracking services: the `Tracker` contract,
  its shared `BaseTracker` implementation, two optional capability interfaces, and the static
  `TrackerManager` registry. TrackSearch and the legacy Storio Track/Chapter ORM types used
  in some method signatures are out of scope for this forest; only `DomainTrack` (this forest's
  Track) is the type this cell's own contract is written against.
